MODULE: posts/api
FILES: src/app/api/posts/route.ts, src/app/api/posts/[id]/route.ts, src/app/api/categories/route.ts, src/app/api/tags/route.ts, src/lib/slugify.ts
RESPONSIBILITY: post CRUD API endpoints, category/tag read endpoints, slug utility
KEY_FILES:
- src/app/api/posts/route.ts: GET list with pagination/filtering/sorting, POST create with auth
- src/app/api/posts/[id]/route.ts: GET/PUT/DELETE single post with auth, cascade delete
- src/app/api/categories/route.ts: GET categories for dropdown
- src/app/api/tags/route.ts: GET/POST tags for multi-select
- src/lib/slugify.ts: URL-friendly slug generation from title
DEPENDENCIES:
- uses: next-auth: getServerSession for API auth
- uses: @prisma/client: ORM queries with includes
- imports: src/lib/prisma: Prisma singleton
- imports: src/lib/slugify: slugify function
INTERFACES:
- GET /api/posts: list with ?page, ?limit, ?status, ?sortBy, ?sortOrder — returns {posts, pagination}
- POST /api/posts: create post — requires auth, body: {title, content, slug?, excerpt?, coverImageUrl?, categoryId?, tags?, status?}
- GET /api/posts/[id]: read single post with category, tags, author
- PUT /api/posts/[id]: update post — requires auth, partial body
- DELETE /api/posts/[id]: delete post — requires auth, cascades to PostTag and Comment
- GET /api/categories: list all categories
- GET /api/tags: list all tags
- POST /api/tags: create tag — body: {name}
TRAPS:
- [LOW] Session user id accessed via (session.user as {id?: string}).id cast — next-auth default type lacks id field | FIX: cast to {id?: string} in all API routes
- [LOW] slugify uses regex replace chain — may not handle unicode/emoji correctly | FIX: acceptable for English-only blog content
CHANGELOG:
- root | add: initial posts API with CRUD, pagination, filtering, sorting
